= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [In which year did Pakistan conduct underground nuclear tests in the Chagai Hills, formally declaring itself a nuclear weapons state?], (
  [1974], [1988], [1998], [2001],
))

#mcq(2, [Who led the Awami League in East Pakistan and championed the historic Six-Point Movement demanding regional autonomy in 1970?], (
  [Ziaur Rahman], [Sheikh Mujibur Rahman], [H.M. Ershad], [Maulana Bhashani],
))

#mcq(3, [On which date did the 240-year-old Hindu monarchy formally come to an end in Nepal, declaring it a secular federal republic?], (
  [1990], [April 2006], [May 2008], [September 2015],
))

#mcq(4, [The controversial legislation passed in Sri Lanka in 1956 that recognized Sinhala as the sole official language of administration is known as the:], (
  [Ceylon Independence Act], [Sinhala Only Act], [13th Amendment Act], [Tamil Disfranchisement Act],
))

#mcq(5, [The Indian Peace Keeping Force (IPKF) was sent to Sri Lanka in 1987 under the tenure of Rajiv Gandhi, and was pulled back in 1990 by which Prime Minister?], (
  [Indira Gandhi], [V.P. Singh], [Chandra Shekhar], [P.V. Narasimha Rao],
))

#mcq(6, [Operation Cactus (November 1988) was a swift military intervention conducted by Indian armed forces to save the government of which South Asian nation?], (
  [Sri Lanka], [Bhutan], [Maldives], [Nepal],
))

#mcq(7, [In which city was the South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC) formally established in December 1985?], (
  [New Delhi], [Kathmandu], [Islamabad], [Dhaka],
))

#mcq(8, [Which country was officially inducted as the eighth member state of SAARC at the 14th Summit held in New Delhi in April 2007?], (
  [Myanmar], [Afghanistan], [Maldives], [Mauritius],
))

#mcq(9, [The South Asian Free Trade Area (SAFTA) agreement was signed in 2004 and came into formal legal operation on which date?], (
  [1 January 2004], [1 January 2006], [15 August 2007], [1 January 2010],
))

#mcq(10, [The historic 30-year treaty for sharing the dry-season waters of the River Ganga at the Farakka Barrage was signed between India and Bangladesh in which year?], (
  [1971], [1985], [1996], [2015],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [In late May 1998, Pakistan conducted five nuclear tests in the Chagai Hills of Balochistan in direct response to India's Pokhran-II tests, establishing mutual nuclear deterrence.], answer: [C])

#solution(2, [Sheikh Mujibur Rahman ('Bangabandhu') founded the Awami League and launched the Six-Point Movement in 1966, sweeping the 1970 elections and leading Bangladesh to independence in 1971.], answer: [B])

#solution(3, [On 28 May 2008, the first meeting of Nepal's newly elected Constituent Assembly officially abolished the monarchy, establishing a secular federal democratic republic.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [The Sinhala Only Act of 1956 declared Sinhala as the sole official language of Ceylon, igniting peaceful protests by Tamils and laying the ground for armed civil strife.], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [The IPKF was deployed in 1987 by Rajiv Gandhi; following immense domestic criticism and heavy casualties, it was officially pulled out in March 1990 by Prime Minister V.P. Singh.], answer: [B])

#solution(6, [Operation Cactus was launched on 3 November 1988 by the Indian military to foil an armed coup against Maldivian President Maumoon Abdul Gayoom carried out by Sri Lankan mercenaries.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [SAARC was founded on 8 December 1985 in Dhaka (Bangladesh). Its permanent Secretariat was later established in Kathmandu (Nepal).], answer: [D])

#solution(8, [Afghanistan was formally admitted as the eighth member of SAARC at the 14th New Delhi Summit in April 2007, marking the first expansion of the association since 1985.], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [SAFTA was signed at the 12th SAARC Summit in Islamabad in January 2004 and officially came into force on 1 January 2006 to lower regional customs tariffs.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [Prime Minister H.D. Deve Gowda and Bangladeshi Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina signed the historic 30-year Ganga Water Sharing Treaty at Farakka in December 1996.], answer: [C])

